    culture: "Virginia Beach's birth culture blends military-family practicality with a growing natural birth community shaped by the city's coastal lifestyle. With a large active-duty military population, many families navigate TRICARE benefits alongside local birth support options. The broader Hampton Roads area has seen a rise in community doulas addressing maternal health disparities." ,
    heroLocalDetail: "From the bustling corridor along Virginia Beach Boulevard to the oceanfront neighborhoods near the Boardwalk and Atlantic Avenue, families in Virginia Beach live where suburban sprawl meets coastal charm. The Hilltop area near Laskin Road and the growing Town Center district provide healthcare access and community gathering spots for new parents." ,
    hospitalDetails: [
      { name: "Sentara Virginia Beach General Hospital" , thumbnail: "/images/virginia-beach-va-hospital-sentara-vb-general.webp", address: "1060 First Colonial Road, Virginia Beach, VA 23454" , url: "https://www.sentara.com/hospitalslocations/sentara-virginia-beach-general-hospital" , nicuLevel: "III" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome as support persons" , midwifeFriendly: true, medicaid: true, lactation: true, privateRooms: true, paragraph: "Sentara Virginia Beach General Hospital is a 273-bed Magnet-recognized facility and Virginia Beach's primary tertiary care hospital, home to the region's only Level III Trauma Center. While the Family Maternity Center relocated to Sentara Princess Anne Hospital in 2011, Virginia Beach General continues to provide comprehensive women's health services including gynecologic surgery, a Comprehensive Breast Center accredited by the National Accreditation Program for Breast Centers, and maternal-fetal medicine consultations for high-risk pregnancies. The hospital accepts Virginia Medicaid and most private insurance plans, with lactation support services available through referral. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to prepare for your delivery here." },
      { name: "Sentara Princess Anne Hospital" , thumbnail: "/images/virginia-beach-va-hospital-sentara-princess-anne.webp", address: "2025 Glenn Mitchell Drive, Virginia Beach, VA 23456" , url: "https://www.sentara.com/hospitalslocations/sentara-princess-anne-hospital/medical-services/family-maternity-suite" , nicuLevel: "III" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome; one adult support person may stay overnight" , midwifeFriendly: true, medicaid: true, lactation: true, privateRooms: true, paragraph: "Sentara Princess Anne Hospital is a 174-bed acute care hospital serving southern Virginia Beach and the primary maternity destination for Virginia Beach families, with Family Maternity services relocated here from Virginia Beach General in 2011. The Family Maternity Center features 11 private labor-delivery-recovery rooms, 4 private triage rooms, 2 operating rooms, 24 private postpartum rooms, and a Specialty Level III NICU with all-private rooms including special rooms for twins. Ranked by U.S. News & World Report among the nation's best for maternity care (2022-2023), the center offers 24-hour board-certified obstetrician, anesthesiologist, and neonatologist coverage. The hospital supports skin-to-skin contact, delayed cord clamping, rooming-in, and natural birth options, and earned the 2024 IBCLC Care Award and Lactation Team Daisy Award for breastfeeding support. Doulas are welcome as support persons, and Virginia Medicaid is accepted. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to prepare for your delivery here." },
      { name: "Naval Medical Center Portsmouth" , thumbnail: "/images/virginia-beach-va-hospital-naval-medical-center.webp", address: "620 John Paul Jones Circle, Portsmouth, VA 23708" , url: "https://portsmouth.tricare.mil/" , nicuLevel: "III" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome; support persons permitted during labor and delivery" , midwifeFriendly: true, medicaid: false, lactation: true, privateRooms: true, paragraph: "Naval Medical Center Portsmouth (NMCP), located across the Elizabeth River in Portsmouth, is the oldest continuously running hospital in the Navy medical system and the primary military treatment facility for Hampton Roads. The hospital delivers approximately 3,500 babies annually with an 18-bed Level III NICU equipped with oscillatory ventilation and nitric oxide therapy for premature and critically ill newborns; over 400 infants are admitted to the NICU each year. NMCP supports evidence-based birth practices including delayed cord clamping, immediate skin-to-skin contact (golden hour), and immediate lactation support by obstetric nurses and certified lactation consultants. The hospital earned a Leapfrog \u201cA\u201d rating for Hospital Safety and Joint Commission Gold Seal accreditation. Care is covered by TRICARE for eligible active-duty service members, retirees, and their families. NMCP was the first military hospital to partner with March of Dimes for NICU family support. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to prepare for your delivery here." }
    ],
