    culture: "Richmond is Virginia\u2019s capital city with a growing birth community anchored by VCU\u2019s academic medical center and Bon Secours\u2019 community hospitals. The city mixes historic neighborhoods with modern development, and families here value both evidence-based care options and community-rooted doula support. Richmond\u2019s birth workers are connected and collaborative, particularly through organizations like Birth Matters RVA." ,
    heroLocalDetail: "VCU Medical Center sits in downtown Richmond at 1250 East Marshall Street, right off I-95 and I-64. accessible from most neighborhoods within 15 minutes but subject to rush-hour bottlenecks on the Downtown Expressway. Bon Secours St. Mary\u2019s Hospital is at 5801 Bremo Road in the Near West End, about 10 minutes from the Museum District and Fan neighborhoods. Richmond\u2019s hot, humid summers and occasional winter ice storms can slow your hospital drive. know your route before you need it. The James River Park System\u2019s trails and the Fan\u2019s tree-lined streets are popular for third-trimester walks." ,
    hospitalDetails: [
      { name: "VCU Medical Center" , thumbnail: "/images/hospitals/richmond-va-vcu-medical-center.webp" , address: "1250 E Marshall St, Richmond, VA 23219" , nicuLevel: "Level IV NICU" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome in labor and delivery" , medicaid: "Yes. accepts Virginia Medicaid" , url: "https://www.vcuhealth.org/services/womens-health/our-services/pregnancy-and-birth/facilities/labor-and-delivery-unit/" , paragraph: "VCU Medical Center is central Virginia\u2019s academic powerhouse. a Level I trauma center with a verified Level IV NICU (stated directly on vcuhealth.org) at the Children\u2019s Hospital of Richmond at VCU. It\u2019s the referral destination for high-risk pregnancies from across the region, with maternal-fetal medicine specialists, 24/7 neonatology, and a high-volume labor unit that sees births from every corner of the Commonwealth. Doulas are welcome, and the academic setting means the care team is used to working with birth plans. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to get your preferences ready." },
      { name: "Bon Secours St. Mary\u2019s Hospital" , thumbnail: "/images/hospitals/richmond-va-bon-secours-st-marys.webp" , address: "5801 Bremo Rd, Richmond, VA 23226" , nicuLevel: "Level III NICU" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome in labor and delivery" , medicaid: "Yes. accepts Virginia Medicaid" , url: "https://www.bonsecours.com/locations/specialty-locations/maternity/st-marys-hospital" , paragraph: "Bon Secours St. Mary\u2019s Hospital at 5801 Bremo Road is Richmond\u2019s most popular community maternity hospital, with a Level III NICU (stated directly on bonsecours.com) and a reputation for a warmer, more intimate birth experience than the academic setting at VCU. The Women\u2019s Center at St. Mary\u2019s offers private labor suites, midwifery options, and lactation support. If you\u2019re delivering here, having your birth plan in hand helps the care team support your preferences from day one. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Download the free birth plan template</a> before your tour." },
      { name: "Chippenham Hospital" , thumbnail: "/images/hospitals/richmond-va-chippenham.webp" , address: "7101 Jahnke Rd, Richmond, VA 23225" , nicuLevel: "Level III NICU" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome, HCA policy typically allows two support persons" , medicaid: "Yes, accepts Virginia Medicaid" , url: "https://www.hcavirginia.com/locations/chippenham-hospital/specialties/womens-care/labor-and-delivery" , paragraph: "Chippenham Hospital, part of the HCA Virginia Health System, offers a robust maternal care program with a Level III NICU. The hospital provides spacious LDRP suites, 24/7 anesthesiology coverage, and a dedicated maternal-fetal medicine team for high-risk pregnancies. Known for efficient triage and short wait times in the obstetric emergency department. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to prepare for your delivery." },
      { name: "Henrico Doctors\u2019 Hospital" , thumbnail: "/images/hospitals/richmond-va-henrico.webp" , address: "1602 Skipwith Rd, Richmond, VA 23229" , nicuLevel: "Level III NICU" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome, two support persons typically allowed" , medicaid: "Yes, accepts Virginia Medicaid" , url: "https://www.hcavirginia.com/locations/henrico-doctors-hospital/specialties/womens-care/labor-and-delivery" , paragraph: "Henrico Doctors\u2019 Hospital is an HCA facility specializing in women\u2019s services with a Level III NICU, a 24-hour obstetric hospitalist program, and dedicated maternal-fetal medicine specialists. The Women\u2019s and Children\u2019s pavilion provides a comfortable, family-centered birth experience with lactation consulting and childbirth education classes. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Download the free birth plan template</a> before your tour." },
      { name: "Johnston-Willis Hospital" , thumbnail: "/images/hospitals/richmond-va-johnston-willis.webp" , address: "1401 Johnston-Willis Dr, Richmond, VA 23224" , nicuLevel: "Level III NICU" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome, HCA policy typically allows two support persons" , medicaid: "Yes, accepts Virginia Medicaid" , url: "https://www.hcavirginia.com/locations/johnston-willis-hospital/specialties/womens-care/labor-and-delivery" , paragraph: "Johnston-Willis Hospital, part of the HCA Virginia Health System, provides comprehensive maternity services with Level III NICU support. The hospital features modern labor and delivery suites, 24/7 neonatal specialist coverage, and a dedicated cesarean section operating room on the L&D floor. Known for its experienced nursing staff and strong lactation support program. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to get your preferences ready." } ],
