    culture: "San Bernardino is the largest city in the Inland Empire by land area, serving as a regional hub for healthcare with two Dignity Health hospitals providing maternity care. The birth community reflects the city's diverse population, with a strong Spanish-speaking doula community and growing Medi-Cal doula enrollment through the PAVE program. The San Bernardino Mountains provide a dramatic backdrop, and families here benefit from the region's expanding birth support infrastructure." ,
    heroLocalDetail: "At 38 weeks in San Bernardino, you're likely planning the drive to either St. Bernardine Medical Center on Highland Avenue or Community Hospital on Medical Center Drive. The 210 and 215 freeways can back up significantly during commute hours. If you're delivering during rush hour, give yourself extra time. especially if you're coming from the mountain communities like Crestline or Running Springs. Shandin Hills Golf Course and the San Bernardino National Forest offer walking trails for those final-weeks strolls." ,
    hospitalDetails: [
      { name: "Dignity Health - St. Bernardine Medical Center" , thumbnail: "/images/sb-hospital-v2.webp" , paragraph: "St. Bernardine Medical Center is a 340-bed acute care hospital serving the Inland Empire with a full obstetrics program. The Baby & Family Center offers educational programs, childbirth classes, and support groups for families. Doulas are generally welcome. confirm current visitor policies during your hospital tour. If you're delivering here, having your birth plan ready makes the whole check-in process smoother. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to get started." , address: "2101 N Waterman Ave, San Bernardino, CA 92404" , url: "https://www.commonspirit.org/find-a-location/dignity-health-st-bernardine-medical-center-3756" , nicuLevel: "III" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome as support persons; confirm current visitor policy during your hospital tour" , medicaid: "Yes, accepts Medi-Cal for obstetric services." },
      { name: "Dignity Health - Community Hospital of San Bernardino" , thumbnail: "/images/community-hospital-san-bernardino.webp" , paragraph: "Community Hospital of San Bernardino is a not-for-profit, award-winning hospital with a dedicated Family Birth Center. For more than a century, this hospital has served local families, working hand in hand with St. Bernardine Medical Center. The Family Birth Center offers maternity tours and classes. Doulas are welcome, and the hospital is especially known for its maternity and behavioral health services. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to get started." , address: "1805 Medical Center Dr, San Bernardino, CA 92411" , url: "https://www.commonspirit.org/find-a-location/dignity-health-community-hospital-of-san-bernardino-3876" , nicuLevel: "II" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome as support persons; confirm current visitor policy during your hospital tour" , medicaid: "Yes, accepts Medi-Cal for obstetric services." },
      { name: "Loma Linda University Children's Hospital" , thumbnail: "/images/loma-linda-university-medical-center.webp" , paragraph: "Loma Linda University Children's Hospital is home to the San Manuel Maternity Pavilion, delivering more than 3,000 babies each year. The Level IV NICU is the largest in the region with the highest designation possible, capable of caring for the most complex premature and critically ill newborns. The hospital ranks in the top 10 percent of California hospitals for low C-section rates and supports the WHO 10 Steps to Successful Breastfeeding. Private labor, delivery, and recovery suites provide a comfortable environment, and the dedicated Obstetrics Emergency Department is available 24/7. Doulas are welcome as part of the birth support team, and the hospital accepts Medi-Cal. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to get started." , address: "11234 Anderson St, Loma Linda, CA 92354" , url: "https://lluch.org/mother-baby" , nicuLevel: "IV" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome as part of the birth support team" , medicaid: "Yes, accepts Medi-Cal for maternity and delivery services." },
      { name: "Arrowhead Regional Medical Center" , thumbnail: "/images/san-bernardino-ca-arrowhead-regional.webp" , paragraph: "Arrowhead Regional Medical Center in Colton is San Bernardino County's public hospital, recognized by U.S. News as a High Performing Hospital for Maternity Care. The Maternal-Child Health department follows a Family Centered Care Model, welcoming and acknowledging the diversity of the community. The hospital has a state-of-the-art NICU for premature and critically ill infants and is designated as a Baby-Friendly Hospital, promoting breastfeeding and skin-to-skin contact. As a county hospital, ARMC accepts Medi-Cal and serves all patients regardless of insurance status. Doulas are welcome as part of the family-centered care model. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to get started." , address: "400 N Pepper Ave, Colton, CA 92324" , url: "https://www.arrowheadregional.org/services/womens-health-services/maternal-child-health/" , nicuLevel: "III" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas welcome as part of the family-centered care model" , medicaid: "Yes, accepts Medi-Cal. As a public hospital, all patients are welcome regardless of insurance status." } ],
