    culture: "Rockville is the county seat of Montgomery County and one of Maryland\u2019s most diverse mid-sized cities, with a birth community that draws from the broader DC metro network. Sitting at the heart of the I-270 biotech corridor, Rockville families have direct access to Adventist HealthCare Shady Grove Medical Center \u2014 one of the busiest maternity hospitals in the DC suburbs \u2014 plus a growing community of independent doulas and home-birth midwives. Maryland Medicaid doula coverage since 2024 has been a meaningful expansion for Montgomery County families, and the city\u2019s diversity means you\u2019ll find doulas serving a wide range of cultural and linguistic communities." ,
    heroLocalDetail: "At 38 weeks in Rockville, you\u2019re probably mapping the drive to Shady Grove Medical Center on Medical Center Drive \u2014 most OB practices in the Rockville\u2013Gaithersburg corridor deliver there. If you\u2019re coming from Rockville Town Center, expect a 10 to 15 minute drive, though I-270 and Route 28 can back up during afternoon rush. Rockville Town Square and the Rock Creek Trail heading south toward DC give you flat, paved walking for those final-weeks strolls \u2014 one of the advantages of being in a walkable suburban hub with trail access." ,
    hospitalDetails: [
      { name: "Adventist HealthCare Shady Grove Medical Center" , thumbnail: "/images/rockville-md-hospital-shady-grove.webp" , paragraph: "Adventist HealthCare Shady Grove Medical Center sits at 9901 Medical Center Drive in Rockville, making it the primary maternity hospital for most Rockville families. The Birth Center features private labor and delivery suites, a Level III NICU verified by the American Academy of Pediatrics, and is Maryland\u2019s first birth center to earn Baby-Friendly designation from the WHO and UNICEF for breastfeeding support. Shady Grove is the only hospital in the state to provide dedicated birth advisors who help expecting mothers create personalized birth plans. The hospital explicitly permits one certified doula during labor \u2014 doulas must check in at the L&D front desk and complete a Doula Consent Form. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to prepare for your delivery here." , nicuLevel: "III" , address: "9901 Medical Center Drive, Rockville, MD 20850" , url: "https://www.adventisthealthcare.com/locations/profile/shady-grove-medical-center/" , doulaPolicy: "One certified doula permitted \u2014 must check in at Labor & Delivery front desk and complete a Doula Consent Form" , medicaid: true },
      { name: "Holy Cross Germantown Hospital" , thumbnail: "/images/rockville-md-hospital-holy-cross-germantown.webp" , paragraph: "Holy Cross Germantown Hospital is about 20 minutes north of Rockville at 19801 Observation Drive, offering a Level II Special Care Nursery for babies who need extra support but not full NICU care. The hospital is part of the Holy Cross Health system \u2014 Maryland\u2019s largest birthing hospital network \u2014 and follows the same maternity visiting guidelines as Holy Cross Silver Spring, including two banded visitors for neonatal unit visits. For Rockville families seeking a smaller, less hectic hospital environment with solid neonatal backup, Holy Cross Germantown is a practical alternative to Shady Grove. <a href='/birth-plan-template/'>Use our free hospital birth plan template</a> to prepare." , nicuLevel: "II" , address: "19801 Observation Dr, Germantown, MD 20876" , url: "https://www.holycrosshealth.org/services/maternity-services" , doulaPolicy: "Doulas permitted as support persons \u2014 two banded visitors allowed during labor and delivery per maternity visiting guidelines" , medicaid: true } ],
