    medicaidNote: "Yes - California's Medi-Cal program covers doula services as a state benefit, with reimbursement rates around $1,587 per pregnancy. Families on Medi-Cal can access doula support through the PAVE (Providing Access and doula Viability through Equity) program. Ask your doula whether they accept Medi-Cal directly." ,
    insuranceNote: "In Rancho Cucamonga, many families have Kaiser Permanente coverage through the nearby Ontario Medical Center. Kaiser members can access contracted doula services at no extra cost for eligible plans. Doula coverage by other private insurers is expanding under California law. Check your specific plan for doula benefits. HSA and FSA funds can help cover out-of-pocket doula costs." ,
    faqs: [
      { q: "How much does a doula cost in Rancho Cucamonga?" , a: "Expect to pay $1,000 to $2,500 for a birth doula in Rancho Cucamonga. Inland Empire rates are generally lower than Los Angeles or Orange County. The median package price is around $1,750. The investment typically covers prenatal visits, labor support, and postpartum check-ins. Download the free birth plan template and start thinking about what matters most to you." },
      { q: "Does Medi-Cal cover doulas in Rancho Cucamonga?" , a: "Yes. California's Medi-Cal program covers doula services, reimbursing around $1,587 per pregnancy through the PAVE program. Kaiser Permanente members may also have access to contracted doula services at no extra cost. Ask your doula upfront whether they accept Medi-Cal directly. Grab the free birth plan template and make sure your doula team knows your preferences." },
      { q: "Which hospitals in Rancho Cucamonga accommodate birth plans?" , a: "San Antonio Regional Hospital in nearby Upland, about 5 miles away, accommodates birth plans and welcomes doulas. It was named a U.S. News Best Hospital for Maternity Care in 2025. Arrowhead Regional Medical Center in Colton also provides maternity care with a Level III NICU. Grab the free birth plan template so you walk in prepared." },
      { q: "Are there birth centers in Rancho Cucamonga?" , a: "Yes. The Natural Birth Place is a freestanding birth center located within Rancho Cucamonga city limits at 1881 Business Center Dr. They offer out-of-hospital birth with licensed midwives, water birth, and comprehensive prenatal and postpartum care. It is one of the Inland Empire's premier birth center options. Grab the free birth plan template to think through your options." },
      { q: "Does True Joy Birthing work with Rancho Cucamonga families?" , a: "True Joy Birthing provides free birth-prep tools for Rancho Cucamonga families. The free birth plan, checklist, and guided walkthrough in the app work for any Rancho Cucamonga birth setting. The app also helps you connect with local doulas and midwives in your area." },
      { q: "What about postpartum support in Rancho Cucamonga?" , a: "Rancho Cucamonga has hospital-based lactation support at San Antonio Regional Hospital. The Inland Empire postpartum doula community is growing, with several certified doulas serving the area. Start your search during pregnancy if you want ongoing postpartum support. Learn more about postpartum doula support." } ],
